{
  "schema": "binario-shared-rules-v1",
  "description": "The rules of the three home-screen widgets both phones run (Android's app/src/main/java/it/binario/app/widget/, the iPhone's WidgetKit extension through BinarioKit's WidgetRules.swift): when an automatic refresh may run and when the next one is due (one or two daily windows on the chosen days, a window ending before it starts goes on after midnight and belongs to the day it starts on, the interval counted from the last refresh, a window start in the hour daylight saving skips moves on with the clocks), the automatic return direction («Mostra il ritorno dalle») and the manual direction that holds until the next change, the train type group of a board row from its operator and line code (a row of no known group is never hidden), which runs the route widget lists (hidden types, the time range, a departed train gone one minute after its departure or, with «fino all'arrivo», kept «In viaggio» until its arrival unless cancelled), which departures the station widget lists (live times only while the data are fresh or aging), when a favourite train is running, which service day a refresh asks for a favourite, what one run of the scheduler does for one widget and when it runs next, the retries of a refresh the user asked for, and how fresh the data of a widget are. Times are railway-local (Europe/Rome); the numbers are contracts/shared-data/v1/widgets-v1.json.",
  "readers": [
    "app/src/test/java/it/binario/app/widget/WidgetRulesContractTest.kt",
    "ios/BinarioKit/Tests/BinarioKitTests/WidgetRulesContractTests.swift"
  ],
